Go's runtime on Radix (ADR 0350). A program starts in the C library's
__mlibc_entry, which calls the runtime's C entry; threads are the C
library's pthreads; locks wait on the C library's futex(); memory comes
from mmap, and memory given back is mapped anew with MAP_FIXED, as mlibc
refuses MADV_DONTNEED; signals go through sigaction with Linux's
ucontext, and the C library's own signals (32 to 34) are left to it;
goroutines are preempted with tgkill; the profiler uses setitimer. The
network poller is the BSDs' kqueue one, on the C library's kqueue and
kevent over Radix's event queue (ADR 0353). The path the program was run
as comes from AT_EXECFN. Dukovo only.

